ing  throwaway characters that don't serve a  significant purpose but the people who  do love sao love it for Kirito the  protagonist and they watch it because  they want to see Kirito being awesome  the creators of sao are fully aware of  this and in this regard they deliver  they give us all the kitty to badassery  that we can handle and the fans who are  into that really love it the one story  arc which shifts away from that is  mother's Rosario although this is  technically not even an actual arc but  just a side story this story shifts the  focus to Asuna and some of the new  friends she meets in new minecraft a lot  of people have praised this Side Story  for changing things up and finally  giving some of the other characters time  to shine but to me personally this side  story felt incredibly contrived we are  suddenly introduced to a bunch of new  characters who are part of a guild known  as the sleeping 9  and we are expected to instantly care  about them but it was all way too fast  the characters received almost no  development apart from Yuki and I just  did not feel any sort of attachment to  these random people who suddenly become  asanas BFFs overnight and this is what  I'm afraid will happen to overlord if we  keep going down the road of dozens of  dozens of new characters constantly  being introduced and the story  gravitating towards them for episodes on  end instead of focusing on the main  characters we love and want to learn  more about like Ines and the Guardians  Overlord is without a doubt the far  superior series to Sao in my opinion but  it is not perfect and I am NOT one of  those people who will pretend that it is  if there is one thing that overlord can  learn from Sao it is that more attention  must be given to the main characters  especially when they are as interesting  as the main cast of overlord I want more  inés more albedo more shouts here more  aura and mata and more Pandora's actor  for the love of but anyway let me know  what 